# The ONE ssh key every constellation app uses to reach this phone's terminal.
# cloud-ide and cloud-watchdog are the first two; anything after them uses this
# same pair rather than minting its own.
#
# DECLARED, NOT GENERATED. A key an app invents at first run cannot be
# provisioned ahead of time: authorized_keys would have to wait for the app to
# exist, be launched, and have its key read off a screen and pasted. Declared,
# this file ships with the env and the private half is baked into the APKs from
# the vault at build time, so a fresh phone works with no setup step.
#
# A public key is not a secret. The private half lives sops-encrypted in
# cloud-vault: A0_keys/providers/android/ssh.secrets.yaml.
ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAICP/TWd0q7KEm29dOrPMX5sEn/8THgsrdHJ1NfPiKElK cloud-constellation@android

# cloud-superapp-mcp on oci-apps (cloud-u-containers infra-api_cloud-superapp-mcp,
# build.json ssh.keys = vault_id_rsa): reaches the phone over the wg0 mesh as
# `ssh phone` (nix, :8024) / `ssh phone-termux` (termux, :8023). Public half only.
ssh-rsa  cloud-superapp-mcp@oci-apps (vault_id_rsa)
